/E (This book describes 4 excellent methods to get started. Some are based on theory, others are more intuitive. If you already have a stronger harnony background, feel free to try the harder methods, and use some of the chords suggested here. If you are just starting, read some of the transcriptions here, try to apply whatever you can understand, and use your ears to start pushing your boundaries. Feel free to email us if you have any questions.)
