/E (PRACTICE: pick your pivot notes on your melody. For each of them, write an extensive list of every possible chord that could include that note; this list will be immense, and will require good knowledge on building voicings. Once you have a complete list, try each option in the context of the melody, and see which chords bring you the desire effect. You may try to apply this idea to each note on the melody, resulting in a crazy reharm, almost like a parody. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
